# Errant Minion's prevention is of "that damage" alone (CR 608.2c, 615.7). Bot1 enchants its own Memnite, so the trigger is Bot1's
# at its own upkeep. On turn 3 Kirol, Attentive First-Year (tapping Memnite and itself) copies the trigger. The copy resolves
# first: Bot1 pays three mana, more than the 2 damage, and is dealt none. The original resolves next: Bot1 declines and is dealt
# all 2 - the 1 the copy's X had left over prevents nothing more (were it a lasting shield of the next 3 damage, Bot1 would be at 19).

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Kirol, Attentive First-Year
Memnite
Errant Minion
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Kirol, Attentive First-Year.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Errant Minion.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Upkeep]
Bot1.Battlefield.Kirol, Attentive First-Year.Activate(Stack.Errant Minion)
Bot1.Choose(Memnite; Kirol, Attentive First-Year)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Stack.Count = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.PayCost(Times: 3)
? Bot1.Life = 20
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Decline
[T3 Bot1.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 18
Bot2.Life = 20
